<title>SWITZERLAND: Swissair and Maersk in new codeshare deal.</title>
<headline>Swissair and Maersk in new codeshare deal.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swissair, a unit of SAirGroup, said it was expanding its cooperation agreement with Denmark's Maersk Air by flying between Geneva and Copenhagen in a codeshare agreement.</p>
<p>Swissair said in a statement that a daily Geneva-Copenhagen flight would be served by a new Maersk Air Boeing 737-500 aircraft and the service is scheduled to begin on October 26.</p>
<p>The two airlines already operate codeshare flights between Zurich and Billund via Frankfurt.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
